## Dependencies & Execution Order

### Phase Dependencies

- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — verification only
- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: No setup dependency — can start immediately
- **User Stories (Phase 3-6)**: All depend on Foundational phase (Phase 2) completion
  - US1, US2, US3 can proceed in parallel after Phase 2
  - US4 is independent (backend-only)
- **Polish (Phase 7)**: Depends on all user stories being complete

### User Story Dependencies

- **US1 (New Session)**: Depends on Phase 2 (T002-T006). No dependency on other stories.
- **US2 (Restore Session)**: Depends on Phase 2 (T002-T006). No dependency on other stories.
- **US3 (Safe Deletion)**: Depends on Phase 2 only for context. Can technically be done independently.
- **US4 (Backend Fix)**: Fully independent — backend only, no frontend dependencies.

### Within Each User Story

- All stories are small (1-3 tasks each)
- No internal model→service→endpoint ordering needed — changes are to existing files

### Parallel Opportunities

- T004 and T005 can run in parallel (different store files)
- T002/T003 are sequential (same file, related logic)
- US1, US2, US3, US4 can all run in parallel after Phase 2
- T017 and T018 can run in parallel

